 $v_3$ and solve for $v_1$ in terms of $v_2$ as \\[v_1 = \\frac{30 - v_3}{5} = \\frac{30 - \\frac{5v_2 + 90}{2}}{5} = \\frac{60 - 5v_2 - 90}{10} = \\frac{-30 - 5v_2}{10} = -3 - \\frac{v_2}{2}.\\]\n\nStep 6: From the equation \\[-v_1 - 2v_2 = 30,\\]we can substitute the expression for $v_1$ and solve for $v_2$ as \\[-(-3 - \\frac{v_2}{2}) - 2v_2 = 30\\]\\[3 + \\frac{v_2}{2} - 2v_2 = 30\\]\\[\\frac{v_2}{2} - 2v_2 = 30 - 3\\]\\[\\frac{v_2}{2} - 2v_2 = 27\\]\\[-\\frac{3v_2}{2} = 27\\]\\[v_2 = -18.\\]\n\nStep 7: Substituting the value of $v_2$ into the expression for $v_3$, we get \\[v_3 = \\frac{5(-18) + 90}{2} = \\frac{-90 + 90}{2} = 0.\\]\n\nStep 8: Substituting the values of $v_2$ and $v_3$ into the expression for $v_1$, we get \\[v_1 = -3 - \\frac{-18}{2} = -3 + 9 = 6.\\]\n\nStep 9: Therefore, the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ that has the smallest magnitude is \\[\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ -18 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\n\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ -18 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}}", "decode_seconds": 19.555965844076127, "draft_calls": 0, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 133, "method": "native_ar", "output_hash": "86f1513d5660c5453859759b461cc948f7dfb4892ee9f0dfd9377c581b52e5fd", "output_token_ids": [8468, 220, 16, 25, 1226, 527, 2728, 279, 24524, 1144, 27148, 7413, 90, 5298, 2619, 92, 220, 16, 26033, 220, 17, 26033, 482, 20, 1144, 408, 90, 5298, 2619, 92, 1144, 15487, 1144, 10590, 13536, 90, 85, 92, 284, 1144, 7413, 90, 5298, 2619, 92, 220, 1954, 26033, 220, 966, 26033, 220, 966, 1144, 408, 90, 5298, 2619, 92, 7255, 60, 1687, 649, 18622, 420, 24524, 439, 1144, 27148, 7413, 90, 5298, 2619, 92, 220, 16, 26033, 220, 17, 26033, 482, 20, 1144, 408, 90, 5298, 2619, 92, 1144, 15487, 1144, 10590, 13536, 90, 85, 92, 284, 1144, 7413, 90, 5298, 2619, 92, 220, 15, 26033, 220, 15, 26033, 220, 15, 1144, 408, 90, 5298, 2619, 92, 489, 1144, 7413, 90, 5298, 2619, 92, 220, 1954, 26033, 220, 966, 26033, 220, 966, 1144, 408, 90, 5298, 2619, 92, 7255, 2595, 8468, 220, 17, 25,